# Lighthouse CI working dirs. `.lighthouseci/` is lhci's own scratch space
# (per-run LHRs + assertion results); `lighthouse-reports/` is the parent of the
# per-form-factor `upload.outputDir`s that the PR-comment step and the workflow
# artifact read (lighthouserc.js). Both are regenerated per run, and a local
# `lhci autorun` otherwise leaves them untracked in the tree.
# Deliberately NOT root-anchored: lhci resolves both against `process.cwd()`,
# so running it from e.g. `apps/www/` writes them there instead.
.lighthouseci/
lighthouse-reports/

# Throwaway pages written into a tracked content dir by an adversarial fixture
# suite and removed on exit (scripts/__tests__/check-docs-brain-snippets.test.sh).
# Ignored so a SIGKILLed run cannot leave one committable in a shared worktree —
# CLAUDE.md's "never `git add -A`" rule exists for exactly this shape.
apps/docs/content/**/__fixture-*.mdx

# Same shape, for the scripts/ type + lint gate's fixture suite
# (scripts/__tests__/check-scripts-typecheck.test.sh). Worse if leaked: the
# probe's last-written body is DELIBERATELY broken — an implicit any — so a
# committed leftover reds `bun run type` for everyone, in exactly the directory
# this gate was added to protect. (The suite's OTHER probe, the un-ignored lint
# one, reds `bun run type` as well as `bun run lint` while it is on disk — the
# ignore here is about what can be COMMITTED, not about what breaks locally.)
#
# ⚠️ Covers only the TYPE probe, and the `.fixture.ts` suffix is what keeps the
# pattern narrow enough to do that. tsgo does not read `.gitignore`, so an
# ignored file is still type-checked; oxlint DOES, and listing that suite's LINT
# probe here made both lint probes report zero findings and exit 0 — a green
# meaning "not scanned", which is precisely what those probes exist to detect.
# The lint probe therefore stays visible to git on purpose. Do not "fix" that.
scripts/zz-*.fixture.ts
